\par \pard\plain \s2\keepn \b\f2\cf2\lang2057 \page {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 #} Introduction}} {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 ${\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 $}
 Introduction}} {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 K} introduction}} {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 +{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 +} 00000}} Introduction
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 
\par Calmira is a complete 16-bit shell that lets you manage files, launch applications and control tasks.  It brings Windows 3.1 up to date with some of the advanced user interface enhancements from the Windows world, and for most people, provides welcome rel
ief from the awkwardness of File Manager.
\par 
\par \pard \s5\qc \{bmc intro1.bmp\}
\par \pard \s5 
\par The installation is simple -- just copy a few files into a directory, and you are ready to go.  If you have used the Windows 95 interface before, you should feel quite at home, but in any case, it won't take long to get used to the new look and feel.

\par 
\par \pard \s5\qc \{bmc intro2.bmp\}
\par \pard \s5 
\par There are many settings and options which you can customise, and if that's not enough, then you can even re-write it (or get someone to do it for you!). Calmira is free and the source code is included in this package.  You are free to modify and redistrib
ute it under the terms of the GNU General Public License, version 2 or later.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s2\keepn \b\f2\cf2\lang2057 \page {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 #} Changes}} {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 ${\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 $}
 What's new in Calmira 2.1}} {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 K} whats new}} {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 +{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 +} 00000}}
 What's new in Calmira 2.2
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 
\par \pard\plain \s3\sa30 \b\f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 {\cf9 Changes since Calmira 2.1}{\cf9 
\par }\pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 
\par \pard\plain \s3\sa30 \b\f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 New features
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 \{bmc b.bmp\} Taskbar can be moved to the top of the screen and resized
\par \{bmc b.bmp\} Files can be copied/moved using cut and paste semantics
\par \{bmc b.bmp\} Start Menu rebuilds more quickly
\par \{bmc b.bmp\} Task Manager can be replaced with a built-in version
\par \{bmc b.bmp\} Taskbar buttons can show the real popup system menu
\par \{bmc b.bmp\} Find Files dialog can perform substring matches
\par \{bmc b.bmp\} Bin has a status bar showing selection details
\par \{bmc b.bmp\} Disk volume labels can be edited
\par \{bmc b.bmp\} Windows 95 keyboard support for Start Menu activation
\par \{bmc b.bmp\} Progress box automatically shows bytes copied, if any 
\par \{bmc b.bmp\} Shortcuts can be brought forward by double clicking on Taskbar
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s3\sa30 \b\f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 Graphics improvements
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 \{bmc b.bmp\} All dialog boxes use the Windows 95 style of tabbed pages
\par \{bmc b.bmp\} Glyphs on OK/Cancel buttons can be turned off from Sys.Properties
\par \{bmc b.bmp\} Start Menu Properties dialog uses new style tool buttons
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s3\sa30 \b\f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 Bug fixes
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 \{bmc b.bmp\} File descriptions can be shown in all window title bars
\par \{bmc b.bmp\} Icon windows can open folders with filename extensions
\par \{bmc b.bmp\} Spacebar and comma key can select objects in icon windows
\par \{bmc b.bmp\} Icons from startdef.bmp are displayed in the right order
\par \{bmc b.bmp\} The Start Menu banner does not disappear after changing icon size
\par \{bmc b.bmp\} Taskbar buttons are not lost after closing Taskbar Properties dialog
\par \{bmc b.bmp\} No exception is raised if the Programs menu is not present
\par \{bmc b.bmp\} %CurrentDrive% variable is available from the Disk Properties dialog
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s3\sa30 \b\f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 {\cf9 Changes since Calmira 2.0}{\cf9 
\par }\pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 
