\par \pard\plain \s3\sa30 \b\f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 Installation
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 Copy all of the above files into a single directory on your hard disk, for example, c:\\Calmira.  Avoid putting these in your Windows directory if possible.
\par 
\par The INI files are constantly modified, so the directory must have write permissions.  If you are using it over a network, you can make Calmira load its settings from the Windows directory.  See the {\uldb Miscellaneous Settings}{\v MiscSettings}
 topic for details.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s3\sa30 \b\f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 3D controls library
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 Calmira requires the Ctl3dv2.dll module which is supplied in a ZIP file.  If you don't already have this file in your \\Windows\\System directory, unzip it to there.  Do not leave Ctl3dv2.dll 
in the same directory as Calmira.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s3\sa30 \b\f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 Setting Calmira as the shell
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 
If you don't need Program Manager any more, you can use Calmira as the Windows shell.  You need to modify the System.ini file in your Windows directory, so make a backup copy of it first.  Look for the [Boot] section, where you will find something like:

\par 
\par {\f5\fs18 [Boot]}{\f5\fs18 
\par }{\f5\fs18 shell=progman.exe}{\f5\fs18 
\par }
\par Comment this out by adding a semi-colon in front of it, and add a line pointing to Calmira, for example
\par 
\par {\f5\fs18 [Boot]}{\f5\fs18 
\par }{\f5\fs18 ;shell=progman.exe}{\f5\fs18 
\par }{\f5\fs18 shell=c:}{\f5\fs18 \\}{\f5\fs18 calmira}{\f5\fs18 \\}{\f5\fs18 calmira.exe}{\f5\fs18 
\par }
\par Restart Windows for the new shell to take effect.  If you encounter problems when loading Windows, reset the shell to Program Manager and see the {\uldb Common Problems}{\v CommonProbs} section for more help.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s3\sa30 \b\f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 Using the Calmira task manager
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 If you are currently using the default Windows Task Manager, you are recommended to change to the one supplied with Calmira.  To do so, add the following entry to System.ini:
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s4 \f5\fs18\cf1\lang2057 [Boot]
\par taskman.exe=c:\\calmira\\ctaskman.exe
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 
\par You need to restart Windows for this setting to take effect.  When Calmira is running, double clicking on the desktop or pressing Ctrl+Esc will invoke the new Task Manager.  If Calmira is not running, then the old Windows Task Manager is loaded instead.

\par 
\par \pard\plain \s3\sa30 \b\f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 Uninstalling
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 Simply delete all the files in the Calmira directory.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s3\sa30 \b\f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 Switching shells
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 
In the Shutdown dialog, you can double click on the computer icon instead of pressing OK.  This will patch System.ini to switch shells between Program Manager and Calmira, and then carry out the shutdown command you selected.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s2\keepn \b\f2\cf2\lang2057 \page {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 #} Upgrading}} {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 ${\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 $}
 Upgrading from previous versions}} {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 K} upgrading; files; icons; whats new; calmira.ini; start.ini; settings; options}} {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 +{\footnote 
\pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 +} 00000}} Upgrading from previous versions
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 
\par \pard\plain \s3\sa30 \b\f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 {\cf9 Upgrading from Calmira 2.0 or 2.1x to Calmira 2.2}{\cf9 
\par }\pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 
\par You should replace all the previous files except the two INI files, both of which are fully compatible with version 2.2.
\par \pard\plain \s3\sa30 \b\f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 
\par {\cf9 Upgrading from Calmira 1.0 to Calmira 2.2}{\cf9 
\par }
\par Replacing files
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 You should replace all the Calmira 1.0 files, {\i except}
 your Start.ini file.  It is important that you replace Calmira.ini because it contains new sections which are required for Calmira 2.2 to work correctly.  You can, if you wish, copy the shortcut sections across and set the NumShorts property in the [Desk
top] sections accordingly.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s3\sa30 \b\f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 Option changes
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 Several unnecessary
 settings have been removed, for example, the option to copy files in the background.  Calmira is permanently configured to use the more powerful settings. Options have only been removed when it is certain that performance on slower computers will not be 
affected.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s3\sa30 \b\f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 {\cf9 General Notes}{\cf9 
\par }\pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 
\par \pard\plain \s3\sa30 \b\f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 Icons
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 When new icons are added to Calmira's executable file, they are sorted by name and the index of existing icons are different.  So i
f your shortcuts or Start Menu items specified an icon index, some of these may need to be modified to show the correct icon again.
\par 
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s2\keepn \b\f2\cf2\lang2057 \page {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 #} QuickTour}} {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 ${\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 $} Quick Tour}}
