\par }MaxHistorySize=24
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 Determines the maximum number of entries in history lists
\par 
\par NormalHintPause=800
\par The number of milliseconds before a popup hint appears in dialog boxes. Icon windows use the separate hint delay setting accessed from the {\uldb File System Properties dialog}{\v FileSystemProp}.
\par {\b 
\par }\pard\plain \s4 \f5\fs18\cf1\lang2057 {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 #} MiscDesktop}}{\b  }{\b [Desktop]}{\b 
\par }DeskGridX=16
\par DeskGridY=16
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 The grid size used by "Line up icons" command in desktop menu
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s4 \f5\fs18\cf1\lang2057 FilePaneCols=4
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 Number of columns in Explorer's file pane
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s4 \f5\fs18\cf1\lang2057 {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 #} MiscDisplay}}{\b  }{\b [Display]}{\b 
\par }FontName=MS Sans Serif
\par FontSize=8
\par FontColor=clBlack
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 The font in icon windows etc.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s4 \f5\fs18\cf1\lang2057 RepaintBeforeHourglass=2
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 This switch controls how Calmira updates the screen before an hourglass is displayed.  A value of 1 repaints Calmira's own windows.  A value of 2 repaints all windows that require updating.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s4 \f5\fs18\cf1\lang2057 {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 #} MiscFileTypes}}{\b  }{\b [File Types]}{\b 
\par }\pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 This section is used by File Properties dialog for unregistered files
\par \pard\plain \s4 \f5\fs18\cf1\lang2057 exe=Program
\par com=MS-DOS program
\par dll=Dynamic link library
\par bat=MS-DOS batch file
\par pif=Program information file
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 
\par \pard\plain \s4 \f5\fs18\cf1\lang2057 {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 #} MiscLayouts}}{\b  }{\b [Layouts]}{\b 
\par }\pard\plain \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\f2 This section controls the dimensions of icon windows when automatic sizin}{\f2 
g is used.  The format is <low>..<high>=<columns>*<rows>.  Calmira uses the number of icons in the window to look up the dimensions to use, for example, a window with 8 icons will use a 3x3 grid.  The lines must be stored in ascending order, so you should
}{\f2  edit this manually instead of using the Advanced page.}{\f2 
\par }\pard\plain \s4 \f5\fs18\cf1\lang2057 0..2=2*1
\par 3..4=2*2
\par 5..6=3*2
\par 7..9=3*3
\par 9..12=4*3
\par 13..16=4*4
\par 17..20=5*4
\par 21..25=5*5
\par 26..30=6*5
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 
\par \pard\plain \s4 \f5\fs18\cf1\lang2057 {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 #} MiscTaskbar}}{\b  }{\b [Taskbar]}{\b 
\par }FontName=MS Sans Serif
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 The standard Taskbar font
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s4 \f5\fs18\cf1\lang2057 MinAppHeight=60
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 The pixel position of minimized icons above the bar
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s4 \f5\fs18\cf1\lang2057 UseMouseHook=1
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 Enables/disables mouse hook for compatibility
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s4 \f5\fs18\cf1\lang2057 HintDelay=800
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 Delay before popup hints appear
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s4 \f5\fs18\cf1\lang2057 ShowNoActivate=1
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 Allows the Taskbar to appear without changing the focus. Turn this off if the Taskbar seems to move behind other windows.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s4 \f5\fs18\cf1\lang2057 24HourFormat=h:mm
\par 12HourFormat=h:mm AM/PM
\par FullDateTime=dddd, mmmm d, yyyy
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 Format for date and time display in the Taskbar's clock.  See the explanation of date/time formats near the end of the topic.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s4 \f5\fs18\cf1\lang2057 AdjustClock=control Date/Time
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 This line runs a command to set your PC's time when you double click on the Taskbar's clock.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s4 \f5\fs18\cf1\lang2057 {\plain \f3\fs16\up6\lang2057 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\fs16\up6 #} MiscSounds}}{\b  }{\b [Sounds]}{\b 
