\par \pard\plain \f3\fs20\lang2057 {\f2 All TTabbedNotebooks have been replaced with the new TTabPanel, which was done as follows:}{\f2 
\par }{\f2 
\par }{\f2 1.  Create a new TTabPanel called TabPanel1.}{\f2 
\par }{\f2 2.  Add a TNotebook to the tab panel, called Notebook1.}{\f2 
\par }{\f2 3.  Create pages for Notebook1.}{\f2 
\par }{\f2 4.  Set the TabPanel's Notebook property to Notebook1. The tabs are automatically updated.}{\f2 
\par }{\f2 5.  Cut and paste the controls from the TTabbedNotebook into the TNotebook.}{\f2 
\par }{\f2 6.  Adjust the widths and alignments if necessary -- TTabPanel has more space inside it.}{\f2 
\par }{\f2 7.  Delete the original}{\f2  TTabbedNotebook and put the new notebook in position.}{\f2 
\par }{\f2 8.  Delete FreePageHandles() from the old notebook's OnChange handler.}{\f2 
\par }{\f2 9.  If there is still code in the handler, assign it to the tab panel's OnChange event.}{\f2 
\par }{\f2 10. If StretchShift was used on the old notebook, change it to the tab panel.}{\f2 
\par }{\f2 
\par }{\f2 All TBitBtns have been replaced with TPicBtn, including those in the}{\f2 
\par }{\f2 IconSel unit.  The procedure was as follows:}{\f2 
\par }{\f2 
\par }{\f2 1.  Open each DFM file in text mode.}{\f2 
\par }{\f2 2.  Replace all occurences of TBitBtn with TPicBtn.}{\f2 
\par }{\f2 3.  O}{\f2 pen the corresponding PAS file.}{\f2 
\par }{\f2 4.  Add the PicBtn unit to the Uses clause.}{\f2 
\par }{\f2 
\par }{\f2 
\par }\pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 TCheckList no longer sets its IntegralHeight to True in the constructor. This is to allow StretchShift to work correctly.
