}\pard\plain \intbl \f3\fs20\lang2057 \row \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 
\par If Calmira's home page has been moved, then you should be able to find the new address through a standard web search engine such as {\f5\fs18 www.altavista.digital.com}.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s3\sa30 \b\f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 FTP
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 Visit a {\uldb Simtel.Net mirror site}{\v Simtel}, and look for a newer version in the /win3/deskenh directory.  Simtel.Net is the first place that Calmira is uploaded to.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s3\sa30 \b\f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 Bulletin boards
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 Check out a local BBS if you've only got a modem.  Calmira should reach popular bulletin boards fairly quickly, and you could ask a friendly BBS to fetch the update if it's available.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s3\sa30 \b\f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 If you don't have access to any of the above...
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 The easiest way is to find someone who does, and ask them politely to help you download the program! You can write to computer magazines, or search through CD-ROM collections. 
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s3\sa30 \b\f2\fs20\cf1\lang2057 For email-only users
\par \pard\plain \s5 \f2\fs20\lang2057 
If you have an email account but no web access, I can mail you a mirror of the web site (as a small zip attachment) if it contains additional information.  You will need Internet Explorer or Netscape Navigator to view the files.  {\cf6 
No program files will be sent as email attachments}.
\par 
